// A linear report: prose and charts read top to bottom, over the storefront model. The
// `## artifact` tag makes this file a report rather than a model; `layout=linear` lays its
// tiles out in one column, and `tiles=[…]` lists them in reading order: text tiles (the
// `##|(markdown)` blocks below, by name) and query tiles (this report's own queries over
// the model's views, declared at the end of the file). It declares no source of its own.
##! experimental.givens
##" One category at a time: how it sells across the year, which brands carry it, and the products that lead it.
##| artifact { layout=linear title="Category review"
  tiles=[
    intro { kind=text },
    "revenue_by_month",
    brands_intro { kind=text },
    "category_top_brands",
    products_intro { kind=text },
    "category_top_products"
  ]
}
|##
import { order_items, products } from "storefront.malloy"

##|(markdown) intro
Pick a **Category** in the controls above and every chart below re-runs for it.
Leave the control empty to read the whole catalog. The monthly trend says which
way revenue is moving.
|##

# description="Narrow to one product category. Leave empty for all"
# label="Category" control=select suggest { source=products dimension=category }
given: CATEGORY :: filter<string> is f''

##|(markdown) brands_intro
The brand ranking says who is behind those numbers.
|##

##|(markdown) products_intro
Last, the best-selling products in the category.
|##

# viz=line
# label="Revenue by month"
# subtitle="Revenue by month for the selected category"
query: revenue_by_month is order_items -> sales_by_month + { where: category ~ $CATEGORY }

# viz=bar
# label="Top brands"
# subtitle="The eight brands with the most revenue in the selected category"
query: category_top_brands is order_items -> top_brands + { where: category ~ $CATEGORY }

# label="Top products"
# subtitle="The ten best-selling products in the selected category"
query: category_top_products is order_items -> top_products + { where: category ~ $CATEGORY }

